# .zolo — NOT YAML: string-first, no quotes needed, indentation-only nesting.

Hosting:
    zMeta:
        title:       Hosting
        icon:        bi-hdd-network
        description: Where and how this app runs

    Header:
        zH2:
            label: Hosting
            color: PRIMARY

    Lead:
        zText:
            content: This app's own zServer answers its pages — the data plane. A separate control plane (wake, sleep, blue-green deploy) can run a whole fleet of apps like this one; that layer is ALPHA and lives in the plugin SDK, not here.

    Config_Table:
        zTable:
            title: This app's config
            columns: [setting, value]
            rows:
                - [App, zConsole]
                - [zMode, zCLI]
                - [Data backend, csv via zData]
                - [ZTERMINAL_MODE, readonly (default)]
                - [Compute driver, LocalProcessDriver (dev)]

    Note:
        _zClass: zConsole-note
        zMD:
            content: Set `ZTERMINAL_MODE: sandbox` in zEnv to let the Snippets panel actually run its Python. A production fleet swaps `LocalProcessDriver` for a registered driver like `k8s` — every caller (wake/sleep/status) stays identical.
